;; FH-ROOT-006 — hydration takes its identity from the wire, adopts, and
;; reports a divergence.
;;
;; IDENTITY IS READ, NOT DERIVED. The server knows what it rendered and says
;; so in the Root Manifest it emits as the container's immediately following
;; element sibling; the client adopts that name rather than deriving one and
;; hoping the two agree. So the fixture's manifest deliberately names an id
;; this root form would NEVER derive — a manifest agreeing with derivation
;; would satisfy every assertion by coincidence and prove nothing. The
;; `:derived-root-id` below is that coincidence, written down so the
;; assertions can rule it out.
;;
;; ADOPTION is proven by NODE IDENTITY, not by text. The server's markup is
;; put into the container, the exact DOM nodes it created are captured, and
;; after hydration those SAME node objects must still be mounted. A root
;; that quietly discarded the server render and client-rendered instead
;; would produce identical text and pass any assertion written about it.
;;
;; The mismatch half needs the same care in the other direction. React's
;; `onRecoverableError` is the only signal here, so a harness that never
;; receives it reports nothing and passes on broken and correct HTML alike.
;; The fixture therefore pins a KNOWN-BAD server body as well as the correct
;; one: the divergent case must produce the diagnostic, and the matching
;; case must produce none. Neither assertion means anything without the
;; other.
;;
;; What React recovers from is bounded, and the boundary is React's own: a
;; text mismatch or a missing / extra / wrong-type element reaches the
;; callback; an ATTRIBUTE-only divergence does not, because React documents
;; that it makes no guarantee to patch attribute mismatches. That row is
;; here so the boundary is pinned as a fact rather than discovered later as
;; a surprise.
{:fh/id "FH-ROOT-006"
 :fh/law
 "v/hydrate-root takes its :root-id and its identifierPrefix from the Root Manifest the server emits as the container's immediately following element sibling — never from a derivation — and ADOPTS the server-rendered markup, the server's own DOM nodes surviving the mount, while a divergence React recovers from is REPORTED as :rf.ssr/hydration-mismatch carrying that root-id, composed over any host :on-recoverable-error and bounded to the adoption window. Identity opts supplied client-side are refused with :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid; server markup with no manifest adjacent is the same diagnostic with {:missing :manifest}; and no SSR artefact on the classpath at all is :rf.error/ssr-artefact-missing naming day8/re-frame2-ssr."

 :view  :greeting
 :props {:name "world"}

 ;; The identity the root ends up with — the manifest's, and NOT the id
 ;; `[greeting {…}]` would derive.
 :root-id :fh.root/from-the-wire
 :derived-root-id :re-frame.freehand.root-views/greeting
 :provenance :manifest

 ;; The manifest the server emits beside the container. `:identifier-prefix`
 ;; is a string the client could not have synthesised: the derived default
 ;; is a function of the root-id, so a `srv6-` prefix can only have come
 ;; from this content.
 :manifest {:rf.root/schema-version 1
            :root-id           :fh.root/from-the-wire
            :identifier-prefix "srv6-"}
 :identifier-prefix "srv6-"

 ;; The server's bytes for `[greeting {:name "world"}]`.
 :server-html "<section id=\"greeting\"><h1 id=\"title\">Hello</h1><p id=\"who\">world</p></section>"

 ;; The matching case: the server's nodes are still the mounted nodes, and
 ;; nothing was reported.
 :match {:adopted true
         :same-nodes ["#greeting" "#title" "#who"]
         :mismatches 0}

 ;; The KNOWN-BAD case — the harness's own proof that it can see anything at
 ;; all. The text under #who disagrees, which is squarely inside what React
 ;; recovers from.
 :divergent-html "<section id=\"greeting\"><h1 id=\"title\">Hello</h1><p id=\"who\">SOMEBODY ELSE</p></section>"
 :divergent {:mismatches-at-least 1
             :operation :rf.ssr/hydration-mismatch
             :where     re-frame.freehand/hydrate-root
             :recovery  :warned-and-replaced
             ;; React's recovery is a REPLACEMENT: the page ends up carrying
             ;; the client's truth, never the server's stale value under a
             ;; tree that disagrees with it.
             :final-text "world"}

 ;; A host callback is composed OVER, never clobbered: the framework emits
 ;; first, then the host's own callback runs.
 :host-callback {:invocations-at-least 1}

 ;; Identity comes from the server. Supplying it client-side is a conflict,
 ;; not an override.
 :identity-opts-refused
 [{:opts {:root-id :fh.root/other}          :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}
  {:opts {:identifier-prefix "mine-"}       :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}
  {:opts {:disambiguator :left}             :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}]

 ;; ... and a container the server DID render, with nothing adjacent to say
 ;; what it rendered it as, has no identity to hydrate under. That is a
 ;; broken server render rather than a client-only load, and it fails loud
 ;; rather than falling back on a guess.
 :no-manifest {:error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid
               :missing :manifest}

 ;; The other absence, and a DIFFERENT one: discovery itself is unreachable
 ;; because the optional SSR artefact is not on the classpath. The
 ;; diagnostic names the coordinate to add.
 :no-ssr-artefact {:error :rf.error/ssr-artefact-missing
                   :maven "day8/re-frame2-ssr"}}
